ices [{:answer/id #uuid "15eee99b-6f3d-515b-9d6f-43471d08138c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673455} {:answer/id #uuid "230a53b5-1e03-589b-9bfa-e8aab4db801a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{2 v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673456} {:answer/id #uuid "34289676-1ab7-572f-bb26-c148fecbd449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{2 v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673458} {:answer/id #uuid "6d330680-f87a-598f-baff-4b5aef3a24f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673468} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1c9a96-4346-5200-9709-5f7174852b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\frac{1}{v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d330680-f87a-598f-baff-4b5aef3a24f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- \\frac{1}{v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673468} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1f997e-32b1-55b8-b31d-21179ff85584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ef82846-a542-551b-9346-5d048c648778" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{y} \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" :question/worked-solution "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{y} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =- v + \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)} \\\\ \\left(- \\frac{1}{v - \\sec{\\left(\\frac{3}{v} \\right)}}\\right)\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a Homogeneous Differential Equation into a Separable Equation Using a Substitution"}]}
